# Project Rules

> NOTE: This is a placeholder distilled from the phase docs (PHASE_01–04).
> Replace it with the exact "Project Rules" block from 00_MASTER_PROJECT.md when
> available — that master block is the source of truth.

## Architecture
- This is a Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind site whose defining
  feature is a SINGLE persistent React Three Fiber `<Canvas>` mounted once in the
  root layout (Phase 4). It must never unmount across navigation.
- Pages do NOT create 3D. They publish small state ("which scene to show") to a
  shared store; a SceneController inside the one canvas reacts to it.
- Heavy 3D is lazy-loaded and Suspense-wrapped so the page shell appears instantly.
- The canvas must throttle/pause its render loop when idle or offscreen.

## Accessibility (acceptance criteria for every phase)
- WCAG AA contrast on all text/background pairs.
- Full keyboard navigation with visible focus rings; logical focus order.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for all animation (GSAP, Lenis, 3D).
- Semantic landmarks: header / nav / main / footer. One `<h1>` per page.
- Alt text on all meaningful images.

## SEO
- Every route exports proper metadata (title + description).

## Engineering
- Package manager is pnpm. Pin dependencies to exact stable versions.
- Before installing 3D libs, confirm React / @react-three/fiber / drei
  compatibility.
- Comment the WHY, especially around the persistent-canvas pattern.
- Stack: three, @react-three/fiber, @react-three/drei, gsap, lenis,
  react-hook-form, zod, @hookform/resolvers. (Sanity + Resend come later.)
